From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:18:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] device: Build ART for the read-barrier collector

The build chose ART's userfaultfd collector, which needs the kernel's
CONFIG_USERFAULTFD. The HackberryPi's kernel has none, so ART fell back to
the read-barrier collector at runtime and rejected the boot image and
every app's and service's odex for the other collector ('read barrier
state mismatch'): each boot compiled the boot image in memory (3 s) and
JIT-compiled the framework (9 s of zygote CPU), system_server ran
services.jar interpreted, and 238 MiB of recompiled code sat in /data.
---
 device.mk | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index d7c60a3..8a6d2de 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -34,6 +34,11 @@ $(call inherit-product, $(SRC_TARGET_DIR)/product/product_launched_with_p.mk)
 # Disable compressed APEX
 OVERRIDE_PRODUCT_COMPRESSED_APEX := false
 
+# ART's userfaultfd collector needs CONFIG_USERFAULTFD, which Deckard's hosts
+# lack: ART falls back to the read-barrier collector and rejects every oat
+# file built for the other one.
+PRODUCT_ENABLE_UFFD_GC := false
+
 # VNDK
 # Android 16 deprecates VNDK, but Halium vendors (e.g. Android 14, ro.vndk.version=34)
 # still require a matching VNDK APEX. Without it linkerconfig aborts with
-- 
